As a Lead, I can see exactly what is happening here. This is a classic Jackson Deserialization mismatch.
Your React frontend is now sending the new, cleaner JSON structure (sending circleName and removing the dates), but your Java backend DTOs are still expecting the old fields (transferDate and circleBranchCode). Because Jackson can't find those old fields in the incoming JSON, it just fills them with null.
To fix this and get your COMMON_REQ payload perfectly clean, we need to update your DTOs to match the new contract.
Here are the updated files.
1. Update the Detail DTO (ProfitLossSummaryDto.java)
We need to remove the transferDate, change the circleBranchCode to a String named circleName, and keep the balance.
package com.fincore.YearEndService.DTO;

import lombok.AllArgsConstructor;
import lombok.Data;
import lombok.NoArgsConstructor;
import java.math.BigDecimal;

@Data
@AllArgsConstructor
@NoArgsConstructor
public class ProfitLossSummaryDto {
    // REMOVED: transferDate
    
    // CHANGED: From Integer circleBranchCode to String circleName
    private String circleName; 
    
    private BigDecimal totalProfitLoss;
}

2. Update your Main Payload DTO
Note: You didn't paste the exact class name for the root payload (it might be called something like YearEndRequestPayloadDto or similar), but you need to update it to match the root fields we changed.
Find the DTO that contains processRunId, processId, etc., and make sure it has createdDate and etlDate instead of processDate or date.
// Inside whichever DTO maps to the root "payload" JSON:
@Data
public class YourMainPayloadDto {
    private Long processRunId;
    private Long processId;
    private String batchId;
    
    // REMOVED: private LocalDate processDate; (or date)
    
    // ADDED: The new dates from the frontend
    private String createdDate;
    private String etlDate;
    
    private BigDecimal totalAmount;
    private Integer totalRecordCount;
    
    // This points to the updated DTO above
    private List<ProfitLossSummaryDto> circleWiseDetails; 
}

3. Optional: Update the Interface and Repository
If you are still using ProfitLossRepository.findProfitLossSummaryGroupedByCircle() somewhere else in your code to generate summaries, you need to update it so it joins with CIRCLE_MASTER to get the name, just like we did earlier.
Update the Interface (IProfitLossSummary.java):
package com.fincore.YearEndService.DTO;
import java.math.BigDecimal;

public interface IProfitLossSummary {
    String getCircleName(); // Changed from getCircleBranchCode()
    BigDecimal getTotalProfitLoss();
